1
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:24,680
(Faceless female corpse - part 1)

2
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,400
Trying on earrings?

3
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:33,240
Just looking.

4
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:35,640
Take them off. They don't suit you.

5
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,520
Really? Are they that bad?

6
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:42,400
Yes! Look at your baby fat!

7
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:44,880
These are too lady-like for you.

8
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:48,000
You're hateful, Emma Hong!

9
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:50,120
That hurts, Elsa Hong!

10
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:51,480
Serve you right for calling me fat.

11
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:54,000
I wouldn't know how much you like them
if I didn't say that.

12
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:55,360
Get them if you like.

13
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:58,280
Look! They're expensive!

14
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:00,800
How much are they? My treat.

15
00:02:01,520 --> 00:02:02,480
Are you serious?

16
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:04,880
Thanks, Sis!

17
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:06,720
Excuse me. Can you wrap this up?

18
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,280
Thank you, Miss Hong.

19
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:10,000
Next time we have new arrival from Italy,

20
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:11,680
I'll call you right away.

21
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:12,560
Thank you!

22
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:14,200
Wait!

23
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:16,960
Thanks!

24
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:17,880
Thank you.

25
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:22,720
You squander your money away.

26
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:25,240
Whenever Daddy pays us our allowance,

27
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:26,600
no wonder you spend it almost right away.

28
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:28,440
So what if we're out of cash?

29
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:31,280
We have this Hong Kong Pass.

30
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:33,640
It'll automatically top up.

31
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:38,000
Look at the time.

32
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:39,480
I better practice the piano,

33
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:41,360
or Mom and Daddy would give me grief.

34
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:43,400
How late can it be? Don't forget,

35
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:46,280
they're going to the hospital's
charity party tonight.

36
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:47,840
They won't be home soon.

37
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:49,760
Piano? What is it? Something you can eat?

38
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:51,360
Thank you.

39
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:52,360
Thanks.

40
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:53,800
Here's your change and receipt.

41
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:54,560
Thank you.

42
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:55,680
Let's go.

43
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:57,480
Bye! Come again.

44
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:02,040
Sis, I'm still worried.

45
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:04,680
Not while I'm here. Come on.

46
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,360
Is that your phone?

47
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:14,800
Hello? Yes...tonight.

48
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:16,560
OK! Bye!

49
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:19,360
Why do you have two phones?

50
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:22,240
How hard is that? Don't fuss.

51
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:24,920
Don't tell Mom and Daddy either.

52
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:26,320
Especially Daddy, OK?

53
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:29,080
Don't worry! I took your hush money.

54
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:31,720
Dr. Hong, the operation went well?

55
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:32,440
Very well.

56
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,240
Here's your report.

57
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:34,080
Good. Thanks.

58
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:42,280
This patient should have
their amniocentesis next week.

59
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:47,480
The diabetes report is out for this one.

60
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:48,200
Set up an appointment.

61
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:49,080
OK!

62
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,800
Dr. Hong, I finally get to see you.

63
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:52,760
Mr. Ho!

64
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,960
Yes, thanks for saving my wife and my son.

65
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:58,640
My wife can now breast feed.

66
00:03:58,760 --> 00:03:59,640
Thank you so much.

67
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:02,240
You're welcome.
As long as they're both safe.

68
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:03,800
This is for you...

69
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:06,200
Please take it...
Thank you.

70
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:07,640
Thank you. I'll get out of your way.

71
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:08,560
Right!
Bye!

72
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:10,080
OK! About Mrs. Chan...

73
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:12,520
Mrs. Chan's appointment is tomorrow.

74
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:15,120
Dr. Hong, you overachieved today.

75
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:16,080
It's best to do it today.

76
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:18,320
Dr. Hong, your wife is in your office.

77
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:19,520
What time is it?

78
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:21,480
Almost 6 o'clock.

79
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:23,960
Really? I guess Mrs. Chan can wait.

80
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:25,520
Share the fruits with the others.

81
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:26,400
Thanks.

82
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:27,240
Thanks, Dr. Hong.

83
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:39,240
What's this pretty lady doing in my office?

84
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:43,760
What time is it, Doctor?

85
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:47,600
Looks like someone forgot the time again.

86
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:52,600
I knew it. That's why I came to pick you up.

87
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:56,040
The Director will tell you at the party,

88
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:58,320
you're the best doctor in the hospital.

89
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:02,200
But I'd rather be the best husband
in the world.

90
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:04,520
OK!

91
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:05,280
I'll go change. I won't be long.

92
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:05,920
OK!

93
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:14,400
Hey, hurry up!

94
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:17,440
Hey!

95
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:19,640
Long time no see!

96
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:21,920
I have been so busy.
Drink up...

97
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,920
Finish it...
Cheers...

98
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:36,960
Loser drinks.
Drink up...

99
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:39,320
You are bad. You come here often.

100
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:41,520
We're dead if Daddy found out.

101
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:44,640
I've seen enough of a bar.

102
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:46,000
Let's go home.

103
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:47,400
Hi, Lee!

104
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:49,240
What would you like?

105
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:50,520
The usual for me.

106
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:52,960
A Blue Hawaii for the pretty girl.

107
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:53,720
OK!

108
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:54,520
Thank you.

109
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:57,480
Don't be so boring.

110
00:05:57,560 --> 00:06:00,200
We're OK if we get home before 10 o'clock.

111
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:04,800
You're either home or at the stupid library.

112
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:07,120
I need to show you more of this world.

113
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:08,720
Thank you.

114
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:11,760
Here you go...

115
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:13,120
Thank you.
Enjoy!

116
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:14,360
Cheers!

117
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:20,400
It's quite good.

118
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:21,640
See?

119
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:28,680
Hello? I'm here.

120
00:06:29,080 --> 00:06:32,080
OK! Bye!

121
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:33,680
Who are you talking to?

122
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:36,720
Look at that smile! Boyfriend?

123
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:40,360
Don't be nosy! I'm not telling you.

124
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:42,360
You said sisters should have no secrets.

125
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:43,200
Come on, tell me!

126
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:44,040
You want to know?

127
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:46,880
OK, finish this and I'll tell you.

128
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:48,120
Hi, Ken!

129
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:49,120
Hey!

130
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:49,920
I'll be right back.

131
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:51,120
Drain the glass before I get back.

132
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:52,760
Cheers...

133
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:54,480
Hey!

134
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,280
Hey!

135
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:58,680
She has an open mind.

136
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:06,200
I got something for you.

137
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:07,960
Thanks.

138
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:10,760
What is that?

139
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,680
Police! Hit the lights and kill the music.

140
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:13,720
Who's in charge?

141
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:16,080
Please cooperate. Get your ID cards ready.

142
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:16,920
Follow me!

143
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:22,360
What now?

144
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,040
Climb down!

145
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:28,840
Go!

146
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,040
It's so high!

147
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:31,480
We're dead if you don't.

148
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,040
Police! Open the door!

149
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:38,200
Anyone in there?

150
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,080
Anyone?

151
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:45,680
Elsa, grab my bag!

152
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:49,280
Anyone inside? Open the door!

153
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:51,120
Get the key!

154
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:54,200
Answer me! Anyone inside?

155
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:57,840
I got something for you.

156
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:58,880
That good?

157
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,440
Open up!

158
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:03,520
Madam, the key!

159
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:04,200
Thanks.

160
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:08,000
Check the toilets.

161
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:09,000
Right!

162
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:13,800
Watch out!

163
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:21,480
Come back...

164
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:07,040
You're home! Everything OK?

165
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:08,480
Are you OK?

166
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:14,160
Listen up, both of you!

167
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:17,560
You're grounded for a week.

168
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,520
Felix, don't do this.

169
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:24,160
Don't defend them.

170
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:26,240
How many times did I tell them?

171
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:29,000
Stay away from places with
undesirable characters.

172
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,360
You know bars are off limits.

173
00:09:30,800 --> 00:09:32,080
They just don't listen.

174
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:37,960
Hong Ka-lam, don't take that attitude
with me!

175
00:09:39,760 --> 00:09:40,600
Stop!

176
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:44,760
Hong Ka-lam, stay right there.

177
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:46,520
What attitude is this?

178
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:48,480
See?

179
00:09:49,680 --> 00:09:51,560
How many times have you been to a bar?

180
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:55,160
When did you set a tracker on my phone?

181
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:56,520
That's outrageous!

182
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:57,880
You're outrageous!

183
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:00,560
I let you go the first couple of times.

184
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:02,040
But you keep going back.

185
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:03,640
This time, you even brought your sister.

186
00:10:03,920 --> 00:10:04,880
You want to get the family in trouble?

187
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:06,800
I wasn't getting anyone in trouble.

188
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:08,880
I'm old enough to be in a bar.
What's the problem?

189
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,160
No problem?

190
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:12,480
It's clearly stated in the house rules.

191
00:10:12,560 --> 00:10:13,480
No bars!

192
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:16,040
Bars have undesirable characters
who will attract the Police.

193
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:17,560
You almost got busted today

194
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:19,080
because you don't have an ID.

195
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:20,800
If you got busted,

196
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:21,880
you'll bring the cops to our front door.

197
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:23,760
Your Mom...overstayed her visa.

198
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:25,280
She'll get busted too. Then what?

199
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:27,840
Are you worried about Mom getting busted?

200
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:29,880
Or you don't want to go to jail?

201
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:32,320
You broke the law from the start.
You didn't want to go to jail.

202
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:34,040
Why must Elsa and I be punished for it?

203
00:10:34,160 --> 00:10:36,160
All my life, I'm cooped up in my room.

204
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:37,520
It's a jail sentence.

205
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:39,920
Don't you think you're being selfish?

206
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:41,360
Who's being selfish now?

207
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:42,600
You don't like going to jail?

208
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:44,160
I'll put you in jail.

209
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:46,320
I'll lock you in your room for a week. Move!

210
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:48,200
I'm not going. Let go...
Come on...

211
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:49,760
No!
Move it...

212
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:52,120
I'm not going. You do this every time.

213
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:53,360
No one ever has any say.

214
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:56,240
You're a selfish, control freak.

215
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:57,320
Shut up!

216
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:04,840
Get in...

217
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:06,840
If you won't admit your mistake
after a week,

218
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,640
you'll be locked up until you do.

219
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:12,280
Let me out! You have no right to lock me up!

220
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:14,040
You self-centered, control freak!

221
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:16,040
Let me out!

222
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:19,120
Felix, don't do this.
The punishment is too harsh.

223
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:20,760
Don't try to defend her.

224
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:23,480
Listen, other than food,

225
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:24,440
don't open the door for any reason.

226
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:25,960
Don't let her out.

227
00:11:30,080 --> 00:11:31,520
What happened to your hand? Let me see...

228
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:34,000
Just a small cut...

229
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,880
Small cut? Look at the wound!

230
00:11:36,760 --> 00:11:37,880
Mia, take her to my study.

231
00:11:38,040 --> 00:11:39,880
I'll be with you after I lock
the balcony door. Go!

232
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:17,680
Don't worry, it'll sting a bit.

233
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:22,440
You think Daddy is overbearing and despotic?

234
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:25,760
All your life, whatever you want to learn,

235
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:27,120
wherever you want to go,

236
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:29,320
I never stopped you.

237
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:31,640
You always got what you wanted.

238
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:35,000
I only want you to follow some simple rules

239
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:37,560
so you won't blow your cover.

240
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:39,240
Is it really that hard?

241
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:42,000
You're beginning to misbehave

242
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:44,680
and you're picking up your sister's
bad habits.

243
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:46,960
And you went to a dangerous place today.

244
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:51,960
Well? Does it still hurt?

245
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:57,680
Maybe not you. But your Mom is hurting.

246
00:12:58,880 --> 00:13:00,240
Sorry, Mom!

247
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:03,640
Daddy did this for your own good.

248
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:07,400
Daddy, I'm in on it as well.

249
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:09,320
Don't blame everything on Emma.

250
00:13:09,760 --> 00:13:12,080
I wanted to know what a bar looks like.

251
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:14,080
That's why she took me there.

252
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:17,440
If you want to go, you should have told me.

253
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:18,960
You're old enough to know

254
00:13:19,040 --> 00:13:22,920
places where you should and should not go.

255
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:27,320
OK, get up.

256
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:34,000
Stay off spicy or deep-fried food,
shrimps and crabs.

257
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:35,320
Your Mom should know.

258
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,520
You think I'm ferocious?

259
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:42,640
I shouldn't lock up your sister?

260
00:13:44,760 --> 00:13:47,240
You feel bad about this?

261
00:13:50,280 --> 00:13:52,960
Anything you wish to say to me? Or ask me?

262
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:57,400
I have always wanted to ask one thing.

263
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:01,320
Why can't Emma and I have an ID card?

264
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:04,680
Did you and Mom get married overseas?

265
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:11,040
Twenty years ago,

266
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:15,800
Mom and Daddy met in a private member club.

267
00:14:16,160 --> 00:14:17,720
I was a singer then.

268
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:29,640
(Wise men say only fools rush in)

269
00:14:32,400 --> 00:14:44,280
(but I can't help falling in love with you)

270
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:53,600
(Like a river flows surely to sea)

271
00:14:54,120 --> 00:14:57,480
(Darling, so it goes)

272
00:14:57,680 --> 00:15:03,480
(some things are meant to be)

273
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:10,920
(Take my hand)

274
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:17,200
(Take my whole life too)

275
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:31,720
(for I can't help falling in love with you)

276
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:46,640
(for I can't help falling in love with you)

277
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:57,000
Police! Who's in charge?

278
00:15:57,400 --> 00:15:59,440
Sir! Madam! What is it? I'm the manager.

279
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:01,400
We're looking for illegal workers.

280
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:03,360
What illegal workers?

281
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:06,080
Summon your staff
and ask them to get their ID cards ready.

282
00:16:24,880 --> 00:16:25,600
Mia?

283
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:30,360
Sorry! Why do you look so scared?

284
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:31,840
Is something wrong?

285
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:33,080
No.

286
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:38,760
Some of your colleagues
were arrested for not having a working visa.

287
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:40,240
You don't have one either?

288
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,760
You saw through me.

289
00:16:43,760 --> 00:16:45,880
Looks like I won't get away this time.

290
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:50,120
I'm a doctor.

291
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:51,760
A doctor won't arrest anyone.

292
00:16:54,440 --> 00:16:57,240
A doctor? That's an honest profession.

293
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:00,960
You must look down on
illegal workers like me.

294
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:02,480
Why would I?

295
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:05,600
I think everyone must have a reason

296
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,560
for doing what they did.

297
00:17:08,280 --> 00:17:09,600
I don't think you wanted this to happen.

298
00:17:09,760 --> 00:17:10,960
You must have ineffable reasons, right?

299
00:17:13,320 --> 00:17:14,960
Actually, when I came to Hong Kong,

300
00:17:15,040 --> 00:17:16,880
I was happy to find a good job.

301
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:19,960
But my boss ran away.

302
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:24,240
Luckily, a friend found me
this part-time job.

303
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:27,440
I needed to stay longer to make more money.

304
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:30,880
Now I have overstayed.

305
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:34,120
You're so pretty and such a good singer,

306
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:37,280
I'm sure someone will hire you
for a permanent job.

307
00:17:37,520 --> 00:17:39,320
Madam, please give me a chance.

308
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:40,040
Police!

309
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:42,520
I only wanted to make money.

310
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:45,200
I have two kids to support.

311
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:54,040
Why is it we're like in the movies?

312
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:57,040
I wonder how this plot will end.

313
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:18,520
What is it? You're not feeling well?

314
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:20,640
Sorry!

315
00:18:25,520 --> 00:18:26,200
Well?

316
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:30,400
Oh dear, a life is at stake.

317
00:18:33,240 --> 00:18:35,720
I'm just kidding. I'm thrilled.

318
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:38,040
We're going to be parents.

319
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:45,200
But we can't get married.

320
00:18:49,360 --> 00:18:51,080
Even if we don't register to get married,

321
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:52,840
we can still have children.

322
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:56,280
Our home is big enough for us.

323
00:18:56,480 --> 00:18:58,520
The whole family can live here.

324
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:00,640
But I can't go to the hospital.

325
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:01,880
How can I have the baby?

326
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:04,880
Have you forgotten I'm a doctor?

327
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:06,760
I can deliver a dozen babies for you.

328
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:11,280
Without a birth certificate,

329
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:12,960
the baby won't have an ID card.

330
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:17,160
We can live without an ID card.

331
00:19:17,560 --> 00:19:20,040
I'll do my best to protect you.

332
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:24,080
The question is are you willing

333
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:25,960
to spend the rest of your life with me

334
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:28,840
and build a family.

335
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:36,920
I personally delivered you both.

336
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:40,640
I dare say I love you

337
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:43,280
as much as any other father.

338
00:19:43,840 --> 00:19:45,720
To protect you,

339
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:48,720
that's why I set the rules for you.

340
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:50,320
After all these years,

341
00:19:50,520 --> 00:19:52,000
we're doing rather well.

342
00:19:52,320 --> 00:19:54,800
That means our rules worked.

343
00:19:54,960 --> 00:19:57,200
I know, unlike other kids

344
00:19:57,320 --> 00:20:00,240
you and your sister can't go to school.

345
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:03,360
So we taught you at home.

346
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:06,800
Any extra-curricular activities you like,

347
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:09,280
I will try my best to let you learn.

348
00:20:14,760 --> 00:20:15,520
Let's see...

349
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:18,800
When you're sick, I make you well
and look after you.

350
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:21,400
Bye...
Thanks.

351
00:20:21,520 --> 00:20:22,600
I gave your Mom a supplementary card

352
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:25,000
and I gave you and your sister cash

353
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:26,880
and this Hong Kong Pass to make purchases

354
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,960
that does not require an ID card.

355
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:32,480
So far, no one has doubted you.

356
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:34,000
That's brilliant. You can make
your own purchase.

357
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:35,920
There's still something I don't understand.

358
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:41,120
If Mom admits to the Government
she's an overstayer,

359
00:20:41,360 --> 00:20:42,920
she'll be sent back to her place of origin

360
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:44,560
and then apply to come to Hong Kong again.

361
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:46,560
Emma and I can get our ID cards.

362
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:47,840
We won't have to do this.

363
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:49,440
Right, Mom?

364
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:06,920
Elsa, everyone has a reason for doing
what they did.

365
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:09,880
If Mom doesn't want to talk about it,

366
00:21:10,520 --> 00:21:11,840
she must have a reason.

367
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:17,440
I hope you can understand, OK?

368
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,800
Help! Anyone out there?

369
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:30,520
I can't open the door!

370
00:21:30,720 --> 00:21:31,920
Elsa, don't be scared.

371
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:33,320
Let me think of something.

372
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:36,560
Elsa...I'm here!

373
00:21:39,840 --> 00:21:41,680
Sis...

374
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,320
Elsa, don't be scared.

375
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:44,720
Before Mom and Daddy come home,

376
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:46,760
I'll stay with you.

377
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:49,120
If Mom and Daddy saw me visiting you,

378
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:50,320
you'll get thrown in jail too.

379
00:21:50,360 --> 00:21:51,080
You should hurry back.

380
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:54,680
Don't worry! Daddy gave me seven days.

381
00:21:54,840 --> 00:21:56,760
I can leave the room, I just can't go out.

382
00:21:56,880 --> 00:21:59,520
Even if Daddy knew I visited you,

383
00:21:59,640 --> 00:22:01,040
he'll just extend my sentence.

384
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:03,120
I'm staying here with you tonight.

385
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:04,800
Once upon a time, there were
two little pigs.

386
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:06,280
A fat one and a thin one.

387
00:22:06,360 --> 00:22:07,960
Then the big bad wolf shows up.

388
00:22:08,040 --> 00:22:09,040
Guess which one he'll eat first?

389
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:10,080
The fat one.

390
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:13,800
If you were not in this house,

391
00:22:13,920 --> 00:22:15,480
I'd really go crazy.

392
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:19,200
Actually, Daddy has a point.

393
00:22:19,520 --> 00:22:21,400
How could you take his side?

394
00:22:21,560 --> 00:22:24,200
Daddy lets us go everywhere we want.

395
00:22:24,320 --> 00:22:26,040
He just didn't want us to go somewhere

396
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:28,680
the Police is likely to check our ID cards.

397
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:32,520
Hong Ka-yee, you have been brainwashed

398
00:22:32,600 --> 00:22:34,440
like in a cult.

399
00:22:34,640 --> 00:22:35,840
Let's not talk about this.

400
00:22:36,040 --> 00:22:38,400
Remember I tossed my backpack in a fit?

401
00:22:38,520 --> 00:22:40,520
Did Daddy go through my things?

402
00:22:51,040 --> 00:22:52,400
Did Daddy go through my things?

403
00:22:52,840 --> 00:22:55,280
Worried about your secret phone?

404
00:22:55,560 --> 00:22:58,040
Relax! I hid it.

405
00:22:58,080 --> 00:22:58,960
You're brilliant!

406
00:22:59,080 --> 00:22:59,760
You bet.

407
00:23:00,360 --> 00:23:05,720
When did he put a tracker in my phone?

408
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,840
Luckily, this morning

409
00:23:08,080 --> 00:23:10,480
I reset a super long password.

410
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:12,760
He won't be able to unlock my phone again.

411
00:23:13,040 --> 00:23:14,120
You should talk.

412
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:16,000
You didn't tell me about your secret phone

413
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:18,040
and about your boyfriend.

414
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:20,560
I have people I want to meet
and things I want to do.

415
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:23,000
Never mind...you won't understand.

416
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:26,080
Why not? I saw at the bar

417
00:23:26,160 --> 00:23:28,080
you were quite chummy with that guy.

418
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:29,640
Is he your boyfriend?

419
00:23:29,760 --> 00:23:31,920
You defied Daddy because of the dude?

420
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:34,640
Where are you going? Answer me!

421
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:39,320
A "dude"? That's rather vulgar.

422
00:23:39,400 --> 00:23:40,560
Don't let Daddy hear you.

423
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:41,840
Or he'll say I'm a bad influence

424
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:43,120
and give me a longer sentence.

425
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:45,080
I don't live in a cave.

426
00:23:45,200 --> 00:23:46,760
I go online and watch TV.

427
00:23:46,880 --> 00:23:48,240
I pick up a few terms, what's the big deal?

428
00:23:48,360 --> 00:23:50,120
Don't change the subject.

429
00:23:50,280 --> 00:23:51,560
Is he your boyfriend?

430
00:23:51,720 --> 00:23:53,560
You're such a nosy parker!

431
00:23:54,560 --> 00:23:56,080
You're such a genius.

432
00:23:56,200 --> 00:23:58,680
You played dumb in front of Mom and Daddy.

433
00:23:58,800 --> 00:24:00,240
Look how sneaky you are now.

434
00:24:00,360 --> 00:24:01,840
Nothing compared to you.

435
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:03,480
I've been asking you a question,

436
00:24:03,640 --> 00:24:04,840
you still haven't answered me.

437
00:24:04,960 --> 00:24:06,680
I don't want you to tell on me.

438
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:08,280
Am I a snitch?

439
00:24:08,440 --> 00:24:10,880
If Daddy were to extort a confession
with torture,

440
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:12,800
you'll spill the beans on me.

441
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:15,840
Torture? That's crazy!

442
00:24:15,920 --> 00:24:18,520
Oh my...you're calling me crazy?

443
00:24:18,600 --> 00:24:20,280
You're ready to spread your wings?

444
00:24:20,440 --> 00:24:23,280
Yes, I'm ready to fly.

445
00:24:24,160 --> 00:24:26,200
(A week later)

446
00:24:42,200 --> 00:24:43,440
I just finished my spa.

447
00:24:43,560 --> 00:24:44,720
I'm coming over to you now.

448
00:24:46,040 --> 00:24:47,440
But I have so much to read...

449
00:25:18,440 --> 00:25:19,360
Hi, Elsa!

450
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:22,360
Hi, YY!

451
00:25:22,880 --> 00:25:24,360
I saw you over there just now.

452
00:25:24,520 --> 00:25:25,320
Why did you move?

453
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:28,000
The air con is too cold.

454
00:25:29,720 --> 00:25:31,560
I came looking for you.

455
00:25:33,560 --> 00:25:34,640
Here...

456
00:25:35,960 --> 00:25:37,360
The Sane Cat concert?

457
00:25:37,480 --> 00:25:38,720
The tickets are hard to get!

458
00:25:38,960 --> 00:25:41,440
A friend of a friend got them...for Sunday.

459
00:25:41,720 --> 00:25:44,360
You said you like this band.

460
00:25:45,160 --> 00:25:46,400
I want to know if...

461
00:25:46,520 --> 00:25:48,000
Why? You're busy that day?

462
00:25:48,120 --> 00:25:49,440
You want to sell them?

463
00:25:49,560 --> 00:25:51,040
No...I'm not busy.

464
00:25:51,200 --> 00:25:52,840
I want to ask you to go with me.

465
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:55,400
This Sunday?

466
00:25:55,600 --> 00:25:56,880
Yes, are you busy?

467
00:26:00,040 --> 00:26:01,800
I can't.

468
00:26:01,960 --> 00:26:04,160
Something I need to do at home. Sorry!

469
00:26:04,440 --> 00:26:06,080
But didn't you want to see them live?

470
00:26:06,240 --> 00:26:07,160
Why don't you ask your family...

471
00:26:07,280 --> 00:26:08,640
Sorry! I need to run.

472
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:14,400
Let's go, Mom!

473
00:26:14,640 --> 00:26:16,000
Who's that guy?

474
00:26:16,360 --> 00:26:19,480
Someone I ran into a few times
at the library.

475
00:26:19,600 --> 00:26:20,560
Just a quick chat.

476
00:26:20,800 --> 00:26:22,560
You shouldn't be talking to strangers.

477
00:26:23,040 --> 00:26:25,760
Daddy is worried about you
meeting undesirable characters.

478
00:26:25,920 --> 00:26:27,720
Stay away from strangers.

479
00:26:29,440 --> 00:26:30,880
I'm coming back...

480
00:26:32,240 --> 00:26:33,640
Sorry! I'll talk to you later.

481
00:26:39,360 --> 00:26:40,680
Sorry, I broke it.

482
00:26:42,560 --> 00:26:44,400
It's OK. It's quite old.

483
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:46,440
No, I broke it.

484
00:26:46,640 --> 00:26:48,000
But I don't have cash.

485
00:26:48,160 --> 00:26:49,200
Do you have any electronic account

486
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:50,240
so I can transfer the money?

487
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:53,520
I don't. It's OK. No need to pay me.

488
00:26:53,640 --> 00:26:54,880
No, I broke it.

489
00:26:55,360 --> 00:26:57,360
How about...I buy you a new one.

490
00:26:57,600 --> 00:26:58,600
Next time I see you at the library.

491
00:26:58,680 --> 00:26:59,640
I'll give it to you.

492
00:27:00,480 --> 00:27:02,480
OK. Thanks.

493
00:27:04,840 --> 00:27:06,160
Can you give me your phone number?

494
00:27:06,800 --> 00:27:08,400
Phone number?

495
00:27:08,720 --> 00:27:09,920
Don't get me wrong...

496
00:27:10,040 --> 00:27:11,440
This is not an excuse to get your number.

497
00:27:11,760 --> 00:27:14,480
I wanted to let you choose the color
when I shop for it.

498
00:27:14,920 --> 00:27:16,880
OK!

499
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:26,200
You're Elsa? I'm YY.

500
00:27:26,920 --> 00:27:27,600
Hi!

501
00:27:28,200 --> 00:27:29,240
Hi!

502
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:33,560
This model is in black or white.

503
00:27:33,680 --> 00:27:34,400
What color would you like?

504
00:27:37,760 --> 00:27:39,280
Black, please. Thanks.

505
00:27:41,560 --> 00:27:42,720
You're welcome.

506
00:27:43,040 --> 00:27:46,040
I seem to see you at the library a lot.

507
00:27:46,160 --> 00:27:48,360
Are you in school or working?

508
00:27:52,840 --> 00:27:54,200
I'm in school.

509
00:27:55,600 --> 00:27:57,120
Which one?

510
00:27:59,880 --> 00:28:01,320
HKIU, Hong Kong Island University.

511
00:28:01,480 --> 00:28:03,120
It's my gap year.

512
00:28:04,400 --> 00:28:05,360
That's where I graduated.

513
00:28:06,200 --> 00:28:07,480
Have you tried the dorm canteen?

514
00:28:07,720 --> 00:28:08,960
Is the food still as bad?

515
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:12,120
Can't believe I picked his alma mater.

516
00:28:12,840 --> 00:28:15,280
Better shut up before I give myself away.

517
00:28:18,760 --> 00:28:20,520
Sorry, I have another call.

518
00:28:20,720 --> 00:28:21,760
Talk to you later.

519
00:28:22,360 --> 00:28:24,120
OK! Later...

520
00:28:33,520 --> 00:28:35,080
Notes from the Underground?

521
00:28:36,280 --> 00:28:36,680
Hi!

522
00:28:37,160 --> 00:28:37,720
Hello!

523
00:28:39,120 --> 00:28:41,440
Here...
Thanks.

524
00:28:42,520 --> 00:28:43,880
You bought the upgraded version?

525
00:28:44,040 --> 00:28:46,160
It's expensive. Let me pay you back.

526
00:28:46,360 --> 00:28:48,160
No need. I promised to pay for it.

527
00:28:49,120 --> 00:28:51,240
Thanks.

528
00:28:51,680 --> 00:28:53,640
Can I ask you a question?

529
00:28:54,920 --> 00:28:56,000
I notice you love to read,

530
00:28:56,120 --> 00:28:58,000
but I have not seen you borrow a book.

531
00:28:58,480 --> 00:29:01,520
Really? I see you in the library too.

532
00:29:01,720 --> 00:29:03,480
But I seldom see you read any books.

533
00:29:03,640 --> 00:29:05,560
What are you doing here?

534
00:29:05,760 --> 00:29:09,920
I'm a reporter. I'm here to do research.

535
00:29:10,720 --> 00:29:12,160
You probably didn't notice me.

536
00:29:14,280 --> 00:29:16,000
I need to get to work.

537
00:29:16,440 --> 00:29:17,240
Right!

538
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:45,080
The world is not full of baddies.

539
00:29:45,960 --> 00:29:47,160
What?

540
00:29:47,600 --> 00:29:50,840
Nothing. Where are we going?

541
00:29:51,200 --> 00:29:52,800
Let's go buy something to eat

542
00:29:52,920 --> 00:29:54,120
to cheer your sister up, OK?

543
00:30:00,200 --> 00:30:02,240
Two fruit tarts, please?

544
00:30:02,520 --> 00:30:03,640
Sure! What kind would you like?

545
00:30:03,960 --> 00:30:05,040
Raspberry and mango.

546
00:30:05,160 --> 00:30:06,360
No problem. Just a moment.
Right!

547
00:30:07,720 --> 00:30:09,760
Your sister loves fruit tarts.

548
00:30:09,840 --> 00:30:11,840
This should cheer her up.

549
00:30:11,960 --> 00:30:14,040
She's been locked up for ten days.

550
00:30:14,160 --> 00:30:15,320
That should make anyone crazy.

551
00:30:15,440 --> 00:30:16,560
No food would help.

552
00:30:17,080 --> 00:30:20,600
When I brought her breakfast,

553
00:30:20,800 --> 00:30:22,200
she looks peaky.

554
00:30:22,520 --> 00:30:24,440
I asked her who she met at the bar.

555
00:30:24,600 --> 00:30:25,600
But she wouldn't tell me.

556
00:30:25,920 --> 00:30:28,640
When you went with her last time,

557
00:30:28,840 --> 00:30:30,240
did you meet her friends?

558
00:30:30,480 --> 00:30:33,760
I don't know. It was my first time.

559
00:30:33,880 --> 00:30:36,320
The Police came soon after we arrived.

560
00:30:36,400 --> 00:30:38,400
I asked her when we came home

561
00:30:38,560 --> 00:30:39,880
but she wouldn't tell me.

562
00:30:42,560 --> 00:30:43,920
She wasn't like that before.

563
00:30:44,080 --> 00:30:45,960
She never went drinking.

564
00:30:46,200 --> 00:30:49,880
She must have met someone
who's a bad influence.

565
00:30:50,040 --> 00:30:53,000
Decent people go to bars as well.

566
00:30:53,280 --> 00:30:55,160
The world is not full of baddies.

567
00:30:55,560 --> 00:30:56,880
You should know that, Mom.

568
00:30:57,080 --> 00:30:58,320
What are you talking about?

569
00:30:58,480 --> 00:31:00,880
You met Daddy at a club.

570
00:31:01,240 --> 00:31:02,840
What do you know, kid?

571
00:31:03,160 --> 00:31:05,360
Your fruit tarts are ready.

572
00:31:05,480 --> 00:31:07,240
Great! Thanks.

573
00:31:07,400 --> 00:31:08,520
Thank you.

574
00:31:13,400 --> 00:31:15,400
Hello, Director? The delivery room

575
00:31:15,480 --> 00:31:16,840
has several emergency surgeries.

576
00:31:16,960 --> 00:31:19,280
Can you call Dr. Hong?

577
00:31:19,480 --> 00:31:21,000
You can forget it.

578
00:31:21,120 --> 00:31:22,600
Dr. Hong is busy at home

579
00:31:22,720 --> 00:31:24,480
and took two weeks off.

580
00:31:24,600 --> 00:31:26,600
I'll call other hospitals for you.

581
00:31:27,400 --> 00:31:29,040
This is madness...

582
00:31:29,280 --> 00:31:31,120
Don't think you have won.

583
00:31:31,240 --> 00:31:32,520
Because you haven't.

584
00:31:32,600 --> 00:31:35,680
I won't listen to you anymore.

585
00:31:36,880 --> 00:31:38,360
He's playing the hi-fi?

586
00:31:40,880 --> 00:31:42,000
Just because your music is blaring,

587
00:31:42,040 --> 00:31:43,240
I can still make a lot of noise.

588
00:31:59,160 --> 00:32:01,880
He cut the power? That's so childish!

589
00:32:02,840 --> 00:32:05,560
You think cutting the power will shut me up?

590
00:32:06,120 --> 00:32:08,360
No way. I can make noise with other things.

591
00:32:09,200 --> 00:32:11,680
(So Ti La Ti La So)

592
00:32:12,080 --> 00:32:13,720
(So Ti La Ti La So)

593
00:32:13,800 --> 00:32:14,760
What's going on?

594
00:32:15,080 --> 00:32:16,040
Let's go look upstairs.

595
00:32:16,320 --> 00:32:20,920
(Do Re Mi Fa So La So)

596
00:32:22,640 --> 00:32:24,200
(So La Ti)

597
00:32:24,240 --> 00:32:27,360
(Do Re Mi Do)

598
00:32:27,560 --> 00:32:28,600
Enough of your madness!

599
00:32:28,760 --> 00:32:30,080
Yes, I have gone mad!

600
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:31,560
You made me mad...

601
00:32:31,760 --> 00:32:33,520
(Do Re)

602
00:32:33,720 --> 00:32:35,040
Felix, stop it!

603
00:32:35,360 --> 00:32:37,440
Just ignore her. Go back downstairs...

604
00:32:37,600 --> 00:32:39,400
(So Ti La Ti La So)

605
00:32:39,480 --> 00:32:44,640
(Do, Do Re Mi Fa So La)

606
00:32:56,320 --> 00:32:58,120
(Three weeks later)

607
00:32:58,440 --> 00:33:01,440
Emma...she's eating less and less.

608
00:33:01,640 --> 00:33:03,520
Mom, why don't you talk to Daddy.

609
00:33:03,640 --> 00:33:05,080
See if he'll let her out sooner.

610
00:33:05,360 --> 00:33:07,200
I'm worried she can't take this much longer.

611
00:33:08,760 --> 00:33:11,680
Felix, this has gone on for a month.

612
00:33:11,960 --> 00:33:13,960
Is it time to let Emma out?

613
00:33:14,240 --> 00:33:16,520
Daddy, I'm sure Emma learnt her lesson.

614
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:17,840
Please let her out.

615
00:33:18,200 --> 00:33:21,120
You think this is the attitude of
someone who learnt her lesson?

616
00:33:21,360 --> 00:33:23,000
I need her to understand

617
00:33:23,200 --> 00:33:26,320
the family will always come first.

618
00:33:26,680 --> 00:33:29,640
At least let her out for a breather.

619
00:33:29,960 --> 00:33:31,440
Don't cave in.

620
00:33:31,760 --> 00:33:33,480
Emma is sneaky.

621
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:36,440
No matter what she says, do not let her out.

622
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:39,520
Aren't you going to the market?

623
00:33:39,600 --> 00:33:40,320
I'll drop you.

624
00:33:40,600 --> 00:33:41,640
OK!

625
00:33:44,920 --> 00:33:47,360
Emma, I'm going to get groceries.

626
00:33:47,560 --> 00:33:50,840
I'll make you lasagna later, OK?

627
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:53,320
Emma?

628
00:33:53,520 --> 00:33:55,160
Never mind her. Let's go.

629
00:33:56,360 --> 00:33:57,920
OK!

630
00:33:59,120 --> 00:34:01,280
Watch your sister for me.

631
00:34:10,080 --> 00:34:11,600
Emma, it's me.

632
00:34:11,840 --> 00:34:14,080
Mom and Daddy went out.

633
00:34:14,200 --> 00:34:16,560
Answer me, OK? I'm worried about you.

634
00:34:19,280 --> 00:34:20,080
Emma!

635
00:34:27,080 --> 00:34:29,200
Emma!

636
00:34:30,600 --> 00:34:32,080
Emma, what's wrong?

637
00:34:32,480 --> 00:34:34,040
My stomach hurts.

638
00:34:34,280 --> 00:34:35,760
You had a relapse?

639
00:34:35,920 --> 00:34:38,520
Maybe. I ran out of meds.

640
00:34:38,640 --> 00:34:39,880
What should I do?

641
00:34:40,200 --> 00:34:42,440
Get some from Daddy's study.

642
00:34:42,560 --> 00:34:44,360
Can you get me some?

643
00:34:44,440 --> 00:34:46,360
Right...hang in there. I'll be right back.

644
00:35:02,400 --> 00:35:03,520
Emma, I got your meds.

645
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:05,960
Hang in there!

646
00:35:08,960 --> 00:35:11,000
I'll pry this open...

647
00:35:19,960 --> 00:35:21,920
I got your meds. Hurry...

648
00:35:22,080 --> 00:35:24,680
Brilliant! I'm free!

649
00:35:25,280 --> 00:35:26,600
I thought you were sick.

650
00:35:27,480 --> 00:35:28,600
Why are you dressed like that?

651
00:35:28,840 --> 00:35:30,440
What are you doing?

652
00:35:30,600 --> 00:35:32,640
Need you ask? Isn't this obvious?

653
00:35:32,760 --> 00:35:34,160
You're running away?

654
00:35:34,280 --> 00:35:35,840
Don't! If Mom and Daddy found out,

655
00:35:35,960 --> 00:35:37,760
they'll kill me. Don't go!

656
00:35:37,920 --> 00:35:40,120
You don't understand. I must do this.

657
00:35:40,240 --> 00:35:41,480
Daddy is unreasonable.

658
00:35:41,600 --> 00:35:43,320
I can't let him lock me up forever.

659
00:35:43,440 --> 00:35:45,560
If I don't run away, I'll never be free.

660
00:35:45,680 --> 00:35:49,480
Just think, I'd be miserable if I stayed.

661
00:35:49,600 --> 00:35:52,840
You don't want me to be miserable, right?

662
00:35:54,400 --> 00:35:56,560
Where did you hide my backpack?

663
00:35:56,800 --> 00:35:58,160
In my room.

664
00:35:58,320 --> 00:36:00,760
Brilliant! You knew to hide it.

665
00:36:01,400 --> 00:36:02,600
Here...
Thank you.

666
00:36:04,840 --> 00:36:06,840
Daddy took my old phone.

667
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:07,880
Do you know where it is?

668
00:36:08,120 --> 00:36:08,960
I don't.

669
00:36:09,200 --> 00:36:10,520
Maybe in the safe?

670
00:36:12,920 --> 00:36:14,520
You know the combination?

671
00:36:15,720 --> 00:36:17,000
Where's the phone?

672
00:36:17,480 --> 00:36:18,720
Forget it!

673
00:36:20,480 --> 00:36:22,520
He put a lot of money inside.

674
00:36:23,120 --> 00:36:25,040
He put in money every month

675
00:36:25,200 --> 00:36:26,720
so he can give us the allowance.

676
00:36:26,880 --> 00:36:28,680
I saw the combination one time.

677
00:36:29,120 --> 00:36:31,000
Where is my phone?

678
00:36:31,240 --> 00:36:33,040
Look again.

679
00:36:33,600 --> 00:36:35,880
Forget it. I still have this one.

680
00:36:36,240 --> 00:36:38,680
Wait! Are you sure about this?

681
00:36:38,960 --> 00:36:40,360
I'm positive.

682
00:36:40,600 --> 00:36:41,720
If Daddy should ask you,

683
00:36:41,880 --> 00:36:42,880
just tell him I feigned an illness

684
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:43,760
to con you into opening the door.

685
00:36:43,920 --> 00:36:45,600
Tell him I'm only borrowing the money.

686
00:36:45,800 --> 00:36:47,480
I'll pay him back as soon as I can.

687
00:36:47,760 --> 00:36:49,280
If you took the money,

688
00:36:49,400 --> 00:36:51,320
God knows what Daddy will do
when he's pissed.

689
00:36:51,520 --> 00:36:53,760
Don't worry. Daddy loves you,

690
00:36:53,840 --> 00:36:55,040
he won't do anything to you.

691
00:36:55,160 --> 00:36:58,360
But you'll earn a good scolding
because of me.

692
00:36:58,560 --> 00:37:00,400
Sorry! Don't worry.

693
00:37:00,520 --> 00:37:02,480
I won't tell anyone about the family.

694
00:37:02,560 --> 00:37:04,120
I will protect you and Mom

695
00:37:04,200 --> 00:37:05,320
and won't get you in trouble.

696
00:37:08,880 --> 00:37:09,440
Dr. Hong!

697
00:37:09,640 --> 00:37:10,320
Yes?

698
00:37:10,600 --> 00:37:11,680
While you were in surgery

699
00:37:11,840 --> 00:37:13,840
your wife called about an emergency.

700
00:37:14,000 --> 00:37:14,920
OK, thank you.

701
00:37:19,680 --> 00:37:21,680
Hello, Mia? What's so urgent?

702
00:37:30,520 --> 00:37:31,960
Don't blame Elsa.

703
00:37:32,880 --> 00:37:34,080
She was worried about Emma,

704
00:37:34,200 --> 00:37:35,720
that's why she opened the door.

705
00:37:35,960 --> 00:37:37,640
I can't believe she'd run away

706
00:37:37,960 --> 00:37:39,720
and took $1M with her.

707
00:37:39,920 --> 00:37:41,960
Why does she need so much money?

708
00:37:42,320 --> 00:37:43,440
You two are close,

709
00:37:43,640 --> 00:37:45,280
you must know where she is.

710
00:37:45,440 --> 00:37:46,800
I really don't.

711
00:37:46,960 --> 00:37:49,520
She just said it was a loan.

712
00:37:49,640 --> 00:37:51,320
She'll pay it back later.

713
00:37:51,480 --> 00:37:54,240
She promised she'll keep our family secret

714
00:37:54,360 --> 00:37:56,320
and won't get us in trouble.

715
00:37:58,920 --> 00:38:00,760
What happened to her?

716
00:38:01,520 --> 00:38:03,480
We were doing so well as a family.

717
00:38:03,880 --> 00:38:06,600
Why must she destroy everything?

718
00:38:07,400 --> 00:38:10,840
I already told you the girls are grown up,

719
00:38:11,240 --> 00:38:13,240
locking them inside the house won't work.

720
00:38:14,360 --> 00:38:16,360
What should we do about Emma?

721
00:38:16,560 --> 00:38:18,280
She's running around with so much cash.

722
00:38:18,400 --> 00:38:19,880
And God knows who she's hanging out with.

723
00:38:21,080 --> 00:38:23,240
She can't go far without an ID card.

724
00:38:24,640 --> 00:38:27,000
I better go find her.

725
00:38:28,040 --> 00:38:29,080
I'll go with you.

726
00:38:34,480 --> 00:38:36,320
(Later that night)

727
00:38:40,960 --> 00:38:42,600
What's the password?

728
00:38:49,840 --> 00:38:51,760
Now it's locked.

729
00:38:53,800 --> 00:38:55,840
We looked all night but couldn't find her.

730
00:38:56,240 --> 00:38:59,000
We dared not ask around and catch
people's attention.

731
00:38:59,400 --> 00:39:00,760
They may call the Police.

732
00:39:07,680 --> 00:39:09,440
What should we do now?

733
00:39:09,800 --> 00:39:12,880
It's dangerous for her to be
out there alone.

734
00:39:13,400 --> 00:39:15,000
I know.

735
00:39:15,680 --> 00:39:18,640
But we've been to places she
usually goes to.

736
00:39:20,560 --> 00:39:24,280
It's late. She must have found
a place to stay.

737
00:39:25,360 --> 00:39:26,800
(Next day after Emma left)

738
00:39:26,840 --> 00:39:29,760
I'll always tell you where I am.

739
00:39:30,200 --> 00:39:31,440
You did not.

740
00:39:33,320 --> 00:39:35,840
(Day 4 after Emma left)

741
00:39:40,480 --> 00:39:43,040
Daddy...

742
00:39:43,920 --> 00:39:44,920
Elsa!

743
00:39:45,440 --> 00:39:46,920
You were home late last night?

744
00:39:47,360 --> 00:39:50,960
Mom and I looked for Emma all night.

745
00:39:51,480 --> 00:39:53,920
Mom just went to bed.

746
00:40:02,320 --> 00:40:05,120
(Day 7 after Emma left)

747
00:40:05,840 --> 00:40:10,240
Happy birthday to you...

748
00:40:10,360 --> 00:40:13,360
Happy birthday to Daddy...
Happy birthday to Felix...

749
00:40:13,600 --> 00:40:16,400
Happy birthday to you.

750
00:40:21,080 --> 00:40:23,720
I already told you the girls are grown up,

751
00:40:23,880 --> 00:40:26,400
locking them inside the house won't work.

752
00:40:26,800 --> 00:40:28,720
I'll lock you in your room for a week. Move!

753
00:40:28,800 --> 00:40:30,280
I'm not going. Let go...
Come on...

754
00:40:30,360 --> 00:40:33,680
No! You're a selfish, control freak.

755
00:40:33,840 --> 00:40:34,720
Shut up!

756
00:40:35,040 --> 00:40:36,240
If you won't admit your mistake
after a week,

757
00:40:36,360 --> 00:40:38,200
you'll be locked up until you do.

758
00:40:40,840 --> 00:40:42,760
Let me out...

759
00:40:42,840 --> 00:40:45,600
When are you letting me out,
you control freak?

760
00:40:45,880 --> 00:40:49,640
Let me out, you control freak.

761
00:40:49,800 --> 00:40:51,480
You're self-centered...

762
00:40:51,560 --> 00:40:55,720
Let me out, control freak...

763
00:40:57,840 --> 00:41:00,560
You are a control freak!

764
00:41:03,720 --> 00:41:04,960
What are you looking at?

765
00:41:05,200 --> 00:41:08,360
I want to see what happened to you.

766
00:41:09,400 --> 00:41:11,480
You did this to me.

767
00:41:11,640 --> 00:41:12,880
You never treated me like a daughter,

768
00:41:12,960 --> 00:41:14,360
or this house as your home.

769
00:41:14,400 --> 00:41:16,120
No father would do this to his daughter.

770
00:41:16,200 --> 00:41:18,760
You think you own the world
and everyone is your slave.

771
00:41:18,840 --> 00:41:21,880
Who doesn't treat this place as a home?

772
00:41:22,360 --> 00:41:23,600
Who's thinking only of herself

773
00:41:23,720 --> 00:41:26,200
with no regard for any consequences
or the family?

774
00:41:26,400 --> 00:41:27,680
Even if this is my home,

775
00:41:27,800 --> 00:41:29,200
does that mean I can't go anywhere

776
00:41:29,280 --> 00:41:30,120
or do anything for the rest of my life?

777
00:41:30,320 --> 00:41:32,880
You have plenty of things to do
and places to go.

778
00:41:33,200 --> 00:41:35,400
But no matter where you are
and what you're doing,

779
00:41:35,520 --> 00:41:37,400
the family must come first.

780
00:41:37,720 --> 00:41:40,840
You must learn to sacrifice yourself
for this family.

781
00:41:42,400 --> 00:41:44,240
I won't listen to your crap anymore.

782
00:41:47,400 --> 00:41:48,840
I knew you'd be rebellious.

783
00:41:49,120 --> 00:41:51,840
That's why I took two weeks off
to watch you,

784
00:41:52,040 --> 00:41:54,200
to ensure you understand
what I'm saying.

785
00:41:54,360 --> 00:41:57,120
Go ahead! You think locking me up
means you have won?

786
00:41:57,400 --> 00:42:00,400
You can lock me up, but not my mind.

787
00:42:00,560 --> 00:42:01,440
Lock me up as long as you want,

788
00:42:01,520 --> 00:42:04,600
but I'll never listen to you again,
control freak...

789
00:42:12,280 --> 00:42:12,920
What is it?

790
00:42:13,160 --> 00:42:13,920
What's wrong?
What is it?

791
00:42:14,080 --> 00:42:15,120
Look at this!

792
00:42:15,520 --> 00:42:17,400
Female corpse found in the New Territories.

793
00:42:17,640 --> 00:42:20,000
Bodies found by hikers is nothing new.

794
00:42:20,200 --> 00:42:21,720
But this time the victim's face

795
00:42:21,880 --> 00:42:23,640
was chewed up by wild boars

796
00:42:23,720 --> 00:42:24,800
leaving behind a bloody mess.

797
00:42:24,880 --> 00:42:26,080
It was a faceless corpse.

798
00:42:26,160 --> 00:42:27,560
She has the same build as Emma.

799
00:42:27,680 --> 00:42:29,160
It suits you. Get it.

800
00:42:29,360 --> 00:42:32,080
Emma has the same top. It's Emma!
